# Production Environment Configuration for Render
# Copy these to Render Dashboard > Environment Variables

# ===================================
# REQUIRED - Set these in Render
# ===================================

# MongoDB Atlas Connection
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster.mongodb.net/kanban?retryWrites=true&w=majority

# Firebase Admin SDK
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project-id
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx@your-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nYour-Private-Key-Here\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"

# CORS - Comma-separated list of allowed frontend URLs
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-nextjs-app.vercel.app,https://www.yourdomain.com

# Frontend App URL (for email links, etc.)
APP_URL=https://your-nextjs-app.vercel.app

# ===================================
# AUTO-CONFIGURED by render.yaml
# ===================================
# These are set automatically, but you can override if needed:
# NODE_ENV=production
# PORT=4001
# JWT_SECRET=<auto-generated-by-render>

# ===================================
# EMAIL CONFIGURATION (Optional)
# ===================================
# Choose ONE email service for notifications

# OPTION 1: Gmail (Recommended for small apps)
# Setup: Enable 2FA, then create app password at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
# EMAIL_SERVICE=gmail
# EMAIL_USER=your-email@gmail.com
# EMAIL_PASS=your-16-char-app-password
# EMAIL_FROM=your-email@gmail.com

# OPTION 2: SendGrid (Recommended for production)
# Free tier: 100 emails/day
# Signup: https://sendgrid.com/
# EMAIL_HOST=smtp.sendgrid.net
# EMAIL_PORT=587
# EMAIL_USER=apikey
# EMAIL_PASS=your-sendgrid-api-key
# EMAIL_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com

# OPTION 3: Mailgun (Good for high volume)
# EMAIL_HOST=smtp.mailgun.org
# EMAIL_PORT=587
# EMAIL_USER=postmaster@yourdomain.mailgun.org
# EMAIL_PASS=your-mailgun-password
# EMAIL_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com

# OPTION 4: Brevo (formerly Sendinblue) - 300 emails/day free
# EMAIL_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
# EMAIL_PORT=587
# EMAIL_USER=your-brevo-email
# EMAIL_PASS=your-brevo-smtp-key
# EMAIL_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com

# OPTION 5: Outlook/Microsoft 365
# EMAIL_HOST=smtp-mail.outlook.com
# EMAIL_PORT=587
# EMAIL_USER=your-email@outlook.com
# EMAIL_PASS=your-password
# EMAIL_FROM=your-email@outlook.com

# ===================================
# CHECKLIST FOR RENDER DEPLOYMENT
# ===================================
#
# MongoDB Setup:
# [ ] Created MongoDB Atlas account
# [ ] Created cluster (free tier M0)
# [ ] Created database user with password
# [ ] Whitelisted all IPs (0.0.0.0/0) in Network Access
# [ ] Copied connection string and added to MONGODB_URI
#
# Firebase Setup:
# [ ] Created/selected Firebase project
# [ ] Enabled Authentication
# [ ] Downloaded service account key (Project Settings > Service Accounts)
# [ ] Copied FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID, FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL, FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY
# [ ] Properly escaped FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY with \n for newlines
#
# Render Setup:
# [ ] Created Render account
# [ ] Deployed from render.yaml (Blueprint) OR manually created Web Service
# [ ] Added all required environment variables above
# [ ] Set ALLOWED_ORIGINS to your frontend URL(s)
# [ ] Deployment successful and service is running
# [ ] Tested /health endpoint: curl https://your-app.onrender.com/health
#
# Frontend Setup:
# [ ] Updated NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL in Next.js to Render URL
# [ ] Deployed frontend to Vercel/other host
# [ ] Verified WebSocket connections work
# [ ] Tested authentication flow
#
# Optional:
# [ ] Configured email service for notifications
# [ ] Set up custom domain in Render
# [ ] Enabled auto-deploy on git push
# [ ] Set up monitoring/alerts
